{{!--
  Dragonbane — the generic card, front.

  The build is that of the other card types, but without their content
  structure: title plaque with the overlapping ornament band, the body below
  it, the second band at the foot, the source reference along the right edge.

    ┌────────────────────────────────┐
    │  ✦───  parchment plaque  ───✦  │  .db-head / .db-title-plaque
    │▀▀▀▀▀ ornament band ▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀│  .db-strip-top (overlaps the plaque)
    │                              ║ │
    │   card text as markdown      ║ │  .db-generic-body
    │                              ║ │
    │▄▄▄▄▄ ornament band ▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄│  .db-strip-bottom
    └────────────────────────────────┘
       ║ = .db-side-ref, along the right edge

  The card deliberately knows ONLY a title and a source as values. Everything
  else — running text, sub-headings, lists, tables AND pictures — the author
  writes as markdown, in the note itself. The body is one place,
  `front-body`, and the card type says what fills it, in order: `content` in
  the block, a `## Vorderseite` section, and failing both the note's own text
  before its first heading. Open a note, write the card.

  The logo comes from the note too: `![[mein-logo.png]]` becomes a real
  `<img>` through card-image.hbs, and where it stands in the text it stands
  on the card. The template embeds NO picture of its own.

  The author steers the pagination as well: what must stay together goes
  between `%% keep-together %%` and `%% /keep-together %%`, a hard break is
  `%% card-break %%`. Both are Obsidian comments, so invisible in the note.
--}}
<div class="card-root card-front dragonbane generic-card generic-front">
  <div class="db-head">
    <div class="db-title-plaque">
      <div class="card-title"><span class="text-scalable">{{slot "front-header-title" plain=true}}</span></div>
      <span class="cs-overflow-counter"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="db-strip db-strip-top"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card-content-container">
    <div class="card-body-scalable">

    {{#if (slot "front-body")}}
    <div class="db-generic-body">{{slot "front-body" markdown="block"}}</div>
    {{/if}}

    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="db-strip db-strip-bottom"></div>

  <div class="db-side-ref">{{slot "front-side-right" markdown=false fallback=(t "side-ref")}}</div>
</div>
